 "text": "Hi, how are you doing these days? Roughly a mile away, so you' safe for now. Hide under the blanket pullover and use it as a pit for your head. Want to be off the cold ground? That's a good idea. Keep a light in your bag just in case it stops raining. Which way are you going? Sure thing. Nod and they' light. Yes, take it down while it' dry. Which do you want carry, the bag with a warm layer inside, or the light layers? Keep an eye on the thunder. If it sounds fast and near, find a spot to stop at each cross road and wait. Which way is the car park? Then head down the hill as fast as you can, walking only if you lose the light. Pick a spot to stop and hide the tent if you can. Which way is the car park?",
